messages:
Alex H: Quick UX poke — on the mobile console the left nav snap is feeling janky between ~520-680px. When you swipe the sidebar it either full-snaps or overlays table content awkwardly. Also seeing table rows create a horizontal scroll at 640px with long cell values. Screenshot attached: https://redwood-screenshots/px1234 :eyes:

Jamal D: I noticed this too in the latest build. The snap threshold seems off — we have a 576px breakpoint in code, but tablets in portrait sit in that gap. Could we consider a soft-collapse into a bottomsheet at 600px instead of a full overlay?

Sophie G: Agree the overlay feels heavy. Bottomsheet is nicer for discoverability on mobile. Implementation notes: make the nav a separate stacking context so table focus/scroll isn't hijacked. Also increase touch targets on the nav items to 44px min.

Maria P: We have product constraints — teams use the nav for quick model switches. If we bottomsheet it, need quick access to recent models and a persistent breadcrumb. Maybe a condensed toolbar at the top when collapsed.

Alex H: Good call. Condensed toolbar + bottomsheet fallback. For the table overflow: can we try wrapping cell content to two lines with an ellipsis after that, and provide long-press tooltip for full value? That reduces horizontal scroll.

Sophie G: Proposed CSS for table wrapper that fixed most of the jank in my local:```css
.table-wrapper {
  overflow-x: auto;
  -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
}
.table-cell {
  display: -webkit-box;
  -webkit-line-clamp: 2;
  -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
  overflow: hidden;
}
```

Sophie G: And a small JS long-press helper for tooltips (mobile can't hover):```js
let timeout;
cell.addEventListener('touchstart', e => timeout = setTimeout(() => showTooltip(cell.textContent), 500));
cell.addEventListener('touchend', () => clearTimeout(timeout));
```

Jamal D: Accessibility nits: ensure the long-press tooltip is keyboard accessible and adds role="tooltip" with aria-hidden toggles. Focus ring should be visible when you tab into a collapsed nav item. Also announce when bottomsheet opens using aria-live.

Maria P: Can we also tweak copy on the condensed toolbar? Current label "Models" is ambiguous on small screens. Suggest "Active model" + small chevron.

Alex H: Makes sense — "Active model" -> draft copy updated in the PR. Will push copy changes to the preview.

QA Bot: Automated visual tests show a regresssion: sidebar z-index vs toast notifications on small viewports. Toasts are appearing underneath the slide-in nav on 580-610px.

Sophie G: I'll add a z-index policy: nav z-index 7000, toasts 7100 when ephemeral. But maybe better: move toasts to top-right on small screens to avoid overlap entirely.

mobile-preview-bot: Preview build deployed: https://preview.redwood/branches/ux/mobile-nav-fix (build 2026.03.23-1345)

Maria P: I'll sanity-check with PMs and update the rollout doc. Action items: Sophie to prototype bottomsheet & tooltip (EOD), Alex to push copy PR, Jamal to mock condensed toolbar + accessibility notes, Maria to confirm product decisions.

Alex H: Thanks all — marking this thread for follow-up in the design sync tomorrow. :thumbsup:
